+    // ============================================================
+    // E230: 90% drift warning (fires once per process).
+    //
+    // Before the existing handle_count+1 / cmp handle_capacity sequence,
+    // check whether the drift has crossed 90% of capacity and, if so, emit
+    // a one-shot warning naming the live handle_count and the capacity.
+    // The fired-flag lives at runtime_context_field_e230_90_warning_fired
+    // (offset 248, set in runtime_context.sio).
+    //
+    // Threshold is hardcoded to floor(4194304 * 9 / 10) = 3774873. A
+    // dynamic 9/10 division would need integer division helpers that the
+    // x86 emitter does not currently expose, and the capacity constant
+    // itself is hardcoded at native_v2_handle_table_capacity_default()
+    // so the 9/10 ratio is a fixed property of this build. If the
+    // capacity ever changes, both values change together.
+    //
+    // Flow (clobbers rcx and rax freely):
+    //   1. Load fired-flag; jnz past this block if already fired.
+    //   2. Stash threshold in rcx so it survives subsequent loads.
+    //   3. Load handle_count into rax (rbx := context BASE as side effect).
+    //   4. mov rbx, rax (rbx = handle_count); mov rax, rcx (rax = threshold).
+    //   5. cmp rbx, rax; JL past fire body when handle_count < threshold.
+    //   6. Fire body: set fired-flag, print "warning[E230] ...", fall
+    //      through to the existing handle_count+1 sequence.
